# oracle: fix baoab with a temperature ramp (Tstart 1.0 to Tstop 2.0 over the run), no zero keyword, in two runs and a reset_timestep:
# per-atom compare of x, v and f (the random draws follow native atom order). Cut down from examples/PACKAGES/baoab/in.baoab_lj.
# oracle-compare: thermo=all atoms=all rel=1e-8 abs=1e-10
# measured with native LAMMPS: max relative error 2e-10 per atom (the ramp and the second run; thermo agrees to 1e-11)
# native: b332f28 built with the installed lmp (EXTRA-FIX)
units lj
atom_style atomic
lattice fcc 0.8442
region box block 0 3 0 3 0 3
create_box 1 box
create_atoms 1 box
mass * 1.0
velocity all create 1.0 54321 loop geom
pair_style lj/cut 2.5
pair_coeff 1 1 1.0 1.0 2.5
neighbor 0.3 bin
neigh_modify delay 0 every 1 check yes
fix 1 all baoab 1.0 2.0 0.5 777
thermo_style custom step temp pe ke etotal press
thermo_modify format float %.15g
thermo 50
timestep 0.005
run 150
reset_timestep 0
thermo 50
run 150
